# Roles and permissions setup checklist (backend)

> Generated by `auth:setup`. Do these steps, tick them, then delete this file. How roles and permissions work: https://github.com/Light-it-labs/lightit-auth-laravel/blob/main/docs/permission.md

- [ ] **Give `User` roles** (`src/Users/Domain/Models/User.php`): add this line inside the class, right after
  `use HasApiTokens;`. It works whether `User` extends `Authenticatable` or, with 2FA, `TwoFactorAuthenticatable`.

```php
use \Spatie\Permission\Traits\HasRoles;
```

- [ ] **Let super admins pass every check** (`src/Shared/App/Providers/AppServiceProvider.php`): add this line at
  the end of `boot()`.

```php
\Illuminate\Support\Facades\Gate::before(static fn (\Lightit\Users\Domain\Models\User $user): bool|null => $user->hasRole(\Lightit\Shared\Roles\RoleManagement::ROLE_SUPER_ADMIN) ? true : null);
```

- [ ] **Run `vendor/bin/pint src/Users/Domain/Models/User.php src/Shared/App/Providers/AppServiceProvider.php`**:
  it turns the fully qualified names above into `use` imports, in this project's import order.
- [ ] **Run `php artisan migrate`** (creates the role and permission tables).
- [ ] **Seed the roles and permissions**: `php artisan db:seed --class=RoleSeeder`. Run it again whenever you add a
  permission to the catalog in `src/Shared/Permissions/`.
- [ ] **Make your first super admin** in `php artisan tinker`, with the email of an existing user:

```php
\Lightit\Users\Domain\Models\User::query()->where('email', 'admin@example.com')->firstOrFail()->assignRole(\Lightit\Shared\Roles\RoleManagement::ROLE_SUPER_ADMIN);
```

Check it worked: signed in as that user, `GET /api/me/permissions` answers `200` with `super-admin` in `roles`, and
`GET /api/roles` lists `admin`, `super-admin` and `user`.

Running `auth:setup` with Roles and Permissions again warns you while `User` still misses `HasRoles`.
